I'm relatively new to the game (at the point where I can get about a
third of the roles past level 20 fairly regularly).  Except for the
occasional and unavoidable tidbit we all encounter from time to time,
I've pretty much discovered everything I know by myself.  But I must
ask this:

What do you call it when you suddenly realize that a really annoying
enemy you had always avoided is actually really useful?

It happens often enough that there ought to be a word for it.  Floating
eyes are the prototypical example; probably the first enemy people have
this experience with.  (I remember once feeling very satisfied when I
trapped a floating eye in a corridor between two boulders.  To be young
and naive again.  Of course I'm probably still young and naive in your
eyes. :)

Today I experienced this again.  There was this one enemy I almost
always avoided whenever it appeared in large numbers.  But today I was
desperate.  Hungry, without food, and not able to pray safely, I
attacked an especially large group of this enemy.  The attack was
successful, I filled my stomach, and went merrily on my way.  I didn't
notice anything unusual until I looked down and realized it was odd for
an Archaeologist to have a strength of 18/06.

Still got a lot to learn, though.  Looking forward to it.

